Peripherals include both on-chip and off-chip/external ones.

A peripheral's type is defined by its interface.
Each peripheral type's interface is represented by a header file.

For each type of peripheral, I have one header for each specific model.
For example, for UART, I have cmsdk_apb_uart.h, ns16550.h, pl011.h.
And the driver API has a model suffix. 
Such as "uart_irq_tx_ready()" -> "uart_irq_tx_ready_cmsdk_apb_uart()".

This is because there can be multiple models of UART on a board.
If I have a single name for a function, such as `uart_init()`, it will
cause linking error when linking multiple UART drivers together.
